    "story": "Serverless compute runs in the Databricks-managed serverless plane, outside the customer's network. A Private Network Gateway (PNG), created inside the workspace's Network Connectivity Configuration (NCC), places a managed network interface in a dedicated /28 subnet of the customer's shared services VPC; Databricks creates and manages it through a cross-account IAM role in the customer's AWS account. Serverless traffic leaves through that interface as if it originated in the VPC, so it follows the VPC's routes: through the Transit Gateway and Direct Connect / Site-to-Site VPN to the corporate data centre's databases, servers and APIs. The workspace VPC is attached to the same Transit Gateway and is not on the serverless path. On AWS, PNG is in Private Preview: Enterprise tier, serverless DBR workloads, exactly one subnet in one availability zone.",
